    "id": "exp-model-r2-2-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": null,
    "prompt": "The mass of a radioactive isotope in milligrams is given by $M=240e^{-0.35t}$ where $t$ is in days. Find the initial mass and the mass after 6 days, rounding to 2 d.p. where appropriate. Then state what the mass becomes as $t\\to\\infty$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "Initial mass $240\\text{ mg}$; after 6 days $29.39\\text{ mg}$; the mass approaches $0\\text{ mg}$.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}M(0)&=240e^{-0.35(0)}\\\\M(0)&=240\\text{ mg}\\end{align*}$$\n$$\\begin{align*}M(6)&=240e^{-0.35(6)}\\\\M(6)&=240e^{-2.1}\\\\M(6)&\\approx29.39\\text{ mg}\\end{align*}$$\nAs $t\\to\\infty$, $e^{-0.35t}\\to0$, so $M\\to0\\text{ mg}$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 25
  },
